The Android app (android/) is based on Komikku
(https://github.com/komikku-app/komikku), licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
Komikku is itself derived from Mihon (https://github.com/mihonapp/mihon),
TachiyomiSY (https://github.com/jobobby04/TachiyomiSY) and Tachiyomi
(https://github.com/tachiyomiorg/tachiyomi), all licensed under the Apache
License 2.0. Copyright notices in files that come from these projects are
retained.

Parts of the MangaDex integration and the reader engine in the Android app
are adapted from Neko (https://github.com/nekomangaorg/Neko), licensed under
the Apache License 2.0. Each adapted file says so in its first line.

The Android app's zoomable reader pages use telephoto
(https://github.com/saket/telephoto) by Saket Narayan, licensed under the
Apache License 2.0.

Both apps use Lucide icons (https://lucide.dev), licensed under the ISC
License.

The Kotatsu backup import in the Android app
(dev.errnolink.tsuzuki.backup.kotatsu) builds on two projects:

- KotatsuApp/kotatsu-parsers (https://github.com/KotatsuApp/kotatsu-parsers),
  licensed under the Apache License 2.0. The manga and chapter id hash and the
  MangaDex url forms follow that project.

- galpt/mk-bkconv (https://github.com/galpt/mk-bkconv). The Kotatsu source to
  Mihon source name map and the Mihon source id derivation are ported from it,
